#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186369769 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129324 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "71ea2c0c-8bcb-5674-a938-4357302d6429" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing a Rotation-Scaling Matrix That Represents a Geometric Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "730e2b8b-1451-51ad-bd2a-40ca7c9a62c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} & -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369771} {:answer/id #uuid "2b10f497-fa87-5f2c-87c1-ba8d257a9554" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3\\sqrt{2} & 3\\sqrt{2} \\\\ -3\\sqrt{2} & -3\\sqrt{2}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369772} {:answer/id #uuid "cfe920ee-91cf-508a-847b-bb3ec48f62c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2\\sqrt{2} & -2\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 2\\sqrt{2} & 2\\sqrt{2}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369773} {:answer/id #uuid "511c1518-2152-5c09-aece-ccfe590a316f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2} & \\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2} & -\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369774} {:answer/id #uuid "443a5ca8-70d6-54a0-98e0-0e7b64be25a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{6} & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{6} \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{6} & -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{6}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369775}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "443a5ca8-70d6-54a0-98e0-0e7b64be25a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{6} & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{6} \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{6} & -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{6}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369775} :answer-field/id #uuid "95113e42-02b3-5065-b438-928ab09d1c6a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369770}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "031a2cb1-243c-5ae8-a8d9-6bc7aa6f524e" :question/math-academy-id "q-140394" :question/problem "![](images/a4/a42ab3804fa207390da60307a2af967d075c0ae7d1dd108f6db809540ffa6e6a.png)\n\nThe vectors $v$ and $Av$ are shown above. If $A$ is a rotation-scaling matrix, then $A=$" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a rotation-scaling matrix, then we can write\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}r & 0 \\\\ 0 & r\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the scale factor and $\\theta $ is the angle of rotation. \n\nAccording to the diagram, $r=\\frac{1}{3}$ and $\\theta =-\\frac{3\\pi }{4}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}r & 0 \\\\ 0 & r\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{6} & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{6} \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{6} & -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{6}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186394207 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129324 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "71ea2c0c-8bcb-5674-a938-4357302d6429" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing a Rotation-Scaling Matrix That Represents a Geometric Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51328703-fbe2-5d04-852e-d6672e539570" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394209} {:answer/id #uuid "b1c1c7d5-d4f2-523a-92d8-2bf34edf6009" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394210} {:answer/id #uuid "f2eacdc8-9970-5269-aa34-69d6b10aca40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394211} {:answer/id #uuid "aba58c5f-7269-5f4e-9e46-bf3c0ffef660" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394212} {:answer/id #uuid "3cb67527-0d4f-5911-a92c-e407ba5f8bab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394213}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "51328703-fbe2-5d04-852e-d6672e539570" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394209} :answer-field/id #uuid "be0b9c50-e64e-58c9-9a7f-a1416b9581d3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394208}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e5b160e6-d77c-511f-89aa-10fd8ad6198f" :question/math-academy-id "q-81586" :question/problem "![](images/8f/8febf6527cbacf1e328dd7d50180deeab66fc29d4b4391de3e85b7db22b4568c.png)\n\nThe vectors $v$ and $Av$ are shown above. If $A$ is a rotation-scaling matrix, then $A=$" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a rotation-scaling matrix, then we can write\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}r & 0 \\\\ 0 & r\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the scale factor and $\\theta $ the angle of rotation. \n\nAccording to the diagram, $r=3$ and $\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}r & 0 \\\\ 0 & r\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186394256 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129323 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c15923f7-ddc0-5012-9645-922ef36cce97" :knowledge-point/title "Sketching the Image of a Vector Under the Action Of a Rotation-Scaling Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e6a683ae-0f3f-503e-87d1-0e7a029b09c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/9f/9f2b2163f62915ab2a88d96b2e9c40fa1ef5db3f869df495dfd92ac839c5cb2c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394258} {:answer/id #uuid "7d40e22f-22a5-5f8d-9463-c6bfe549287d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/4a/4a32401aa57acd25f4004dfc09169d5548c57ac18dfa16b2ebf7715cce0d62e1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394259} {:answer/id #uuid "cecf05d9-088e-5d65-82c2-d7e8d4cbc936" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/d3/d3d205c51ab59448d5146d190a78dc0b291763a8ec3728d1b0e1bd5c476d355c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394260} {:answer/id #uuid "6ff30b0e-49ba-577b-ad30-cc24a0fe0117" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/e4/e4e39acdbed327aa5472278e743c0f6da4a2cf45ca64b971917bc9b38e81a0a5.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394261} {:answer/id #uuid "baa004dd-4376-5e22-845e-dc24346a23e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/18/180232929bc0d2c3e6e1b410fd9ea5f047b0e81fae62a005464442319f6a1d2b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394262}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6ff30b0e-49ba-577b-ad30-cc24a0fe0117" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/e4/e4e39acdbed327aa5472278e743c0f6da4a2cf45ca64b971917bc9b38e81a0a5.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394261} :answer-field/id #uuid "e51414d9-147d-5c81-b876-34c3bdd3b99b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394257}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "4bebbf60-a47c-5b85-9c8e-87fefe6e5ddd" :question/math-academy-id "q-81701" :question/problem "![](images/f9/f9ad045dc1da5464394ae75061ff7b613334c39d6f5a27d5b23eccef13c339c0.png)\n\nConsider the vector $v$ shown above. Find the vector $Av$ given that \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{6} & -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{6} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{6} & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{6}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $A$ is a rotation-scaling matrix. So, we need to find its scale factor and the angle of rotation.\n\nWe can find the scale factor using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\sqrt{det(A)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{6})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{6})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{18}+\\frac{1}{18}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent $A$ as a product of a rotation and a scaling matrix, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}r & 0 \\\\ 0 & r\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain that\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta &=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta &=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⟹\\,\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, in order to find $Av$, we need to rotate $v$ counterclockwise by an angle of $\\frac{\\pi }{4}$  and scale the result by a scale factor of $\\frac{1}{3},$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/fd/fd2fda4038ae2342b37df91a520a58463ce70748c143c6619968da71411aff1c.png)"}]}
